      ******************************************************************
      *  CBACT04C.cut -- COBOL-CHECK TESTSUITE
      *
      *  Testsuite : CBACT04C INTEREST POSTING
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/CBACT04C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  CBACT04C is the most complex batch program in the CardDemo
      *  suite -- the monthly interest poster.  It reads TCATBAL
      *  (transaction-category balances), looks up XREF (account
      *  cross-reference), reads ACCOUNT data, looks up DISCGRP
      *  (interest rate by group), computes monthly interest via
      *  paragraph 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST, writes a TRANSACT record
      *  through 1300-B-WRITE-TX, and updates the ACCOUNT balance
      *  via 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT.  Per AAP Section 0.7.1 this program
      *  requires >=80% line coverage with explicit cases for the
      *  DISCGRP '23' fallback to default-group, the abend pathway,
      *  and the canonical interest-formula output.
      *
      *  AAP Section 0.5.2 mandates TESTCASE coverage of:
      *    1. 0000-TCATBALF-OPEN          (lines 234-250) open
      *    2. 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT      (lines 325-348) read / EOF
      *    3. 1110-GET-XREF-DATA          (lines 393-413) keyed read
      *    4. 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE      (lines 415-440) DISCGRP +
      *       1200-A-GET-DEFAULT-INT-RATE (lines 443-460) fallback
      *    5. 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST       (lines 462-470) the
      *       canonical interest formula
      *           COMPUTE WS-MONTHLY-INT
      *             = (TRAN-CAT-BAL * DIS-INT-RATE) / 1200
      *    6. 1300-B-WRITE-TX             (lines 473-515) TRANSACT
      *       writer
      *    7. 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT         (lines 350-370) ACCOUNT
      *       rewriter
      *    8. 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM          (lines 628-632) LE abend
      *       wrapper
      *
      *  CRITICAL -- "Do not recreate algorithms" rule (AAP 0.10.1)
      *  ---------------------------------------------------------
      *  This testsuite contains the highest risk of inadvertently
      *  re-implementing production logic because CBACT04C carries
      *  the canonical interest formula at line 464-465:
      *      COMPUTE WS-MONTHLY-INT = (TRAN-CAT-BAL * DIS-INT-RATE)
      *                                                     / 1200
      *  Per the user directive (AAP 0.10.1) this test file MUST
      *  NOT contain that COMPUTE.  All expected WS-MONTHLY-INT
      *  values are LITERAL CONSTANTS chosen by the test author from
      *  external arithmetic knowledge.
      *
      *  Source of expected interest values (TC8/TC9/TC10)
      *  -------------------------------------------------
      *  TC8 -- For TRAN-CAT-BAL = $1000.00 and DIS-INT-RATE = 12.00,
      *         external arithmetic (basic mental math, NOT a
      *         re-implementation of the production COMPUTE) yields
      *         WS-MONTHLY-INT = $10.00.  The literal '10' appears
      *         in the EXPECT clause; the production paragraph
      *         performs the COMPUTE itself when PERFORMed.
      *  TC9 -- For TRAN-CAT-BAL = 0 and any non-zero DIS-INT-RATE,
      *         WS-MONTHLY-INT = 0 by the algebraic identity 0*x = 0.
      *  TC10 - For DIS-INT-RATE = 0 and any non-zero TRAN-CAT-BAL,
      *         WS-MONTHLY-INT = 0 by the algebraic identity x*0 = 0.
      *  These three EXPECT literals are NOT a re-implementation of
      *  the production formula; they are author-provided constants
      *  that the production paragraph computes for the test to
      *  observe.  tests/lint/check_no_business_logic.sh enforces
      *  this rule by rejecting any COMPUTE/MULTIPLY/DIVIDE/ADD/
      *  SUBTRACT verb appearing outside BEFORE-EACH/AFTER-EACH.
      *
      *  Field representations (verified in app/cpy/CVTRA01Y.cpy
      *  and CVTRA02Y.cpy)
      *  -------------------------------------------------------
      *    TRAN-CAT-BAL    PIC S9(09)V99   (CVTRA01Y line 9)
      *    DIS-INT-RATE    PIC S9(04)V99   (CVTRA02Y line 9)
      *    WS-MONTHLY-INT  PIC S9(09)V99   (CBACT04C line 168)
      *
      *  COBOL MOVE alignment rules govern these:
      *      MOVE 1000 TO TRAN-CAT-BAL  -> field holds 1000.00
      *      MOVE 12   TO DIS-INT-RATE  -> field holds 12.00
      *      MOVE 0    TO TRAN-CAT-BAL  -> field holds 0.00
      *  Numeric literal 10 then matches WS-MONTHLY-INT = 10.00 by
      *  the same alignment rule when used in EXPECT.
      *
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 limitation -- file I/O stripping
      *  ---------------------------------------------------
      *  The framework's TestSuiteParser strips OPEN / READ / WRITE /
      *  REWRITE / CLOSE statements to bare CONTINUE in the merged
      *  source.  This means production file-I/O verbs do NOT execute
      *  at test time; the file-status fields retain whatever the
      *  testcase prelude MOVEd into them.  Each testcase pre-sets
      *  the relevant file status (TCATBALF-STATUS, XREFFILE-STATUS,
      *  DISCGRP-STATUS, ACCTFILE-STATUS, TRANFILE-STATUS) to drive
      *  the production IF / EVALUATE arms deterministically,
      *  mirroring the canonical convention in CBACT01C.cut and
      *  CBTRN02C.cut.
      *
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 limitation -- READ ... INVALID KEY
      *  -----------------------------------------------------
      *  The framework strips READ verbs and the runner-script awk
      *  pass comments out the INVALID KEY clause-opener and replaces
      *  END-READ. with CONTINUE.  Body statements between INVALID
      *  KEY and END-READ remain as orphan statements that execute
      *  unconditionally after the synthetic CONTINUE.  In CBACT04C
      *  the orphan bodies are DISPLAY-only (lines 375, 397, 418-419)
      *  so they have no observable side effect on EXPECT-able
      *  fields beyond stdout.
      *
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 limitation -- MOCK FILE
      *  ------------------------------------------
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 does NOT support MOCK FILE directives;
      *  only MOCK CALL / MOCK PARAGRAPH / MOCK SECTION are
      *  implemented.  Per AAP Section 0.10.1 MOCK PARAGRAPH /
      *  MOCK SECTION cannot target the program-under-test, so this
      *  testsuite uses ONLY MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'.  File-I/O
      *  determinism is achieved through pre-set WORKING-STORAGE
      *  status fields (the canonical CardDemo convention).
      *
      *  External dependencies mocked or stubbed
      *  ---------------------------------------
      *    * MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD' (per-testcase, Local scope)
      *      replaces the IBM Language Environment abend service
      *      with a no-op CONTINUE body so the test process is
      *      not torn down when 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM is reached.
      *      The runtime stub at tests/stubs/CEE3ABD.cbl is pre-
      *      compiled by the runner and linked into the merged
      *      binary so any unmocked CALL 'CEE3ABD' resolves at
      *      load time and GOBACKs without terminating the test
      *      process.  Production CALL 'CEE3ABD' uses single-quote
      *      delimiters (line 632); the MOCK uses single quotes to
      *      bind the matcher.
      *
      *  Internal CBACT04C paragraphs are NEVER mocked.  Each
      *  TESTCASE PERFORMs a production paragraph LIVE so every
      *  assertion validates side effects of actual production-code
      *  execution (per AAP Section 0.10.1).
      *
      *  Why no testsuite-scope `COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.`:
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser does not recognise
      *  file-scope COPY directives (the parser only recognises
      *  TESTSUITE / TESTCASE / MOCK / EXPECT / VERIFY / BEFORE-
      *  EACH / AFTER-EACH / END-* / CALL / PARA / PARAGRAPH /
      *  SECTION).  The shared STUB-ABEND-STATE EXTERNAL group is
      *  injected by the runner-script awk pass immediately after
      *  the merged source's WORKING-STORAGE SECTION header so the
      *  WS-ABEND-FLAG and WS-ABEND-CODE fields are visible without
      *  an explicit testsuite-scope COPY.
      *
      *  Test categories (14 testcases)
      *  ------------------------------
      *    TC1  - 0000-TCATBALF-OPEN succeeds with status '00'
      *    TC2  - 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT reads TCATBAL record
      *    TC3  - 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT EOF flips END-OF-FILE
      *    TC4  - 1110-GET-XREF-DATA returns matched record
      *    TC5  - 1110-GET-XREF-DATA missing XREF status 23
      *    TC6  - 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE reads DISCGRP OK
      *    TC7  - 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE 23 triggers default
      *           fallback (the AAP-mandated DISCGRP fallback test)
      *    TC8  - 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST $1000 balance 12pct
      *           yields $10.00 (the canonical formula test)
      *    TC9  - 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST zero balance yields zero
      *    TC10 - 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST zero rate yields zero
      *    TC11 - 1300-B-WRITE-TX writes TRANSACT successfully
      *    TC12 - 1300-B-WRITE-TX write error '92' abends
      *    TC13 - 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT rewrites ACCOUNT
      *    TC14 - 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM invokes CEE3ABD stub
      *
      *  Testcase naming -- 72-column constraint
      *  ---------------------------------------
      *  COBOL fixed-format limits source lines to 72 columns.  The
      *  TESTCASE keyword plus the 7-space leading indent consumes
      *  cols 1-17 and the surrounding pair of single quotes
      *  consumes cols 18 and 72, leaving 54 cols for description
      *  text.  Schema-supplied descriptions exceed this; the names
      *  used here preserve the production-paragraph + feature label
      *  while fitting the constraint.
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Sections 0.4.3, 0.5.1, 0.5.2, 0.7.1, 0.10.1, 0.10.2
      *    app/cbl/CBACT04C.cbl           (program under test)
      *    app/cpy/CVTRA01Y.cpy           (TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD)
      *    app/cpy/CVTRA02Y.cpy           (DIS-GROUP-RECORD)
      *    app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy           (TRAN-RECORD)
      *    app/cpy/CVACT01Y.cpy           (ACCOUNT-RECORD)
      *    app/cpy/CVACT03Y.cpy           (CARD-XREF-RECORD)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy (link-time stub state,
      *                                     auto-injected after
      *                                     WORKING-STORAGE SECTION)
      *    tests/stubs/CEE3ABD.cbl        (LE abend stub)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CSUTLDTC.cut (canonical exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBACT01C.cut (batch-program pattern)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBTRN02C.cut (batch-program pattern)
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/TCATBAL-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/XREF-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/ACCT-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/DISCGRP-FIXTURE-A.cpy
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/DISCGRP-FIXTURE-DEFAULT.cpy
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'CBACT04C INTEREST POSTING'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state.  cobol-check 0.2.16
      *  resets MOCK invocation counters automatically; this block
      *  resets the application-level WORKING-STORAGE that the
      *  production paragraphs read or write:
      *
      *    File-status fields (5 of them, one per SELECT clause):
      *      TCATBALF-STATUS, XREFFILE-STATUS, DISCGRP-STATUS,
      *      ACCTFILE-STATUS, TRANFILE-STATUS.  Each testcase
      *      prelude MOVEs '00', '10', '23', or '92' into the
      *      relevant field to drive the production IF/EVALUATE
      *      arms (file-I/O verbs are stripped to CONTINUE so the
      *      runtime never overwrites these fields).
      *
      *    Diagnostic / status overlays:
      *      IO-STATUS / IO-STATUS-04 -- written by 9910-DISPLAY-IO-
      *      STATUS when an error pathway runs.  APPL-RESULT --
      *      written by every paragraph's IF guard to indicate
      *      success (0) or failure (12) against the file-status.
      *
      *    Record buffers (5 of them):
      *      TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD  (CVTRA01Y, 50 bytes)
      *      CARD-XREF-RECORD     (CVACT03Y, 50 bytes)
      *      ACCOUNT-RECORD       (CVACT01Y, 300 bytes)
      *      DIS-GROUP-RECORD     (CVTRA02Y, 50 bytes)
      *      TRAN-RECORD          (CVTRA05Y, 350 bytes)
      *      Cleared so each testcase observes only the writes
      *      performed by the production paragraph under test.
      *
      *    Interest-running totals:
      *      WS-MONTHLY-INT (S9(09)V99) -- target of 1300-COMPUTE-
      *      INTEREST's COMPUTE; cleared so TC8/TC9/TC10 EXPECTs
      *      observe only the production write.
      *      WS-TOTAL-INT (S9(09)V99) -- accumulates monthly amounts
      *      across the main loop.  Cleared so per-testcase ADD
      *      side effects begin from a known baseline.
      *
      *    TRAN-ID counter:
      *      WS-TRANID-SUFFIX (PIC 9(06)) -- incremented by 1300-
      *      B-WRITE-TX before each STRING into TRAN-ID.  Cleared
      *      so TC11/TC12 produce predictable per-test counter
      *      progression.
      *
      *    Loop-control flags:
      *      END-OF-FILE = 'N' -- main-loop terminator; TC3 watches
      *      it flip to 'Y' when the EOF '10' status arrives.
      *
      *    Stub state (visible via the auto-injected COPY STUB-
      *    ABEND-FLAG that the runner-script awk pass emits
      *    immediately after WORKING-STORAGE SECTION):
      *      WS-ABEND-FLAG = 'N' -- flipped to 'Y' by the link-time
      *      CEE3ABD stub, but per the canonical pattern the per-
      *      testcase MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD' CONTINUE intercepts the
      *      call before the link-time stub runs; abend reachability
      *      is asserted via VERIFY MOCK invocation count rather
      *      than via this flag.
      *      WS-ABEND-CODE = 0 -- mirrored from production line 631
      *      (MOVE 999 TO ABCODE) when the production code reaches
      *      the abend wrapper.
      *
      *    System fields:
      *      ABCODE / TIMING -- production 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM
      *      lines 630-631 set TIMING=0 / ABCODE=999; TC14 asserts
      *      these post-states directly.
      *      RETURN-CODE -- implicit special register; reset to
      *      ZERO for deterministic post-test inspection.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE TCATBALF-STATUS
            INITIALIZE XREFFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE DISCGRP-STATUS
            INITIALIZE ACCTFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE TRANFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS-04
            INITIALIZE APPL-RESULT
            INITIALIZE ABCODE
            INITIALIZE TIMING
            INITIALIZE TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD
            INITIALIZE CARD-XREF-RECORD
            INITIALIZE ACCOUNT-RECORD
            INITIALIZE DIS-GROUP-RECORD
            INITIALIZE TRAN-RECORD
            MOVE 0   TO WS-MONTHLY-INT
            MOVE 0   TO WS-TOTAL-INT
            MOVE 0   TO WS-TRANID-SUFFIX
            MOVE 'N' TO END-OF-FILE
            MOVE 'N' TO WS-ABEND-FLAG
            MOVE 0   TO WS-ABEND-CODE
            MOVE 0   TO RETURN-CODE
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- 0000-TCATBALF-OPEN succeeds with status '00'
      *
      *  PERFORMs 0000-TCATBALF-OPEN (CBACT04C.cbl lines 234-250).
      *  Pre-setting TCATBALF-STATUS = '00' drives the production
      *  IF guard at line 237 to its THEN branch:
      *      MOVE 8 TO APPL-RESULT       (line 235, seed)
      *      OPEN INPUT TCATBAL-FILE     (line 236; stripped to
      *                                   CONTINUE by cobol-check)
      *      IF TCATBALF-STATUS = '00'   (line 237)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT   (line 238) <-- success
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE 12 TO APPL-RESULT  (line 240)
      *      END-IF
      *      IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE        (lines 242-243) <-- exits
      *      ELSE PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM (line 248)
      *
      *  TC1 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO TCATBALF-STATUS  -- forces SUCCESS branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by line 235 (-> 8) then
      *                                     line 238 (-> 0).
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    APPL-RESULT = 0 -- the production literal at line 238;
      *                       not recomputed by the test.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- the SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line
      *           243) does not PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM; abend
      *           pathway must not be reached.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 0000-TCATBALF-OPEN succeeds with status 00'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO TCATBALF-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0000-TCATBALF-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            EXPECT TCATBALF-STATUS TO BE '00'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT reads TCATBAL record
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT (CBACT04C.cbl lines 325-348)
      *  with TCATBALF-STATUS = '00' to drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *      READ TCATBAL-FILE INTO TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD (line 326;
      *                                                  stripped to
      *                                                  CONTINUE)
      *      IF TCATBALF-STATUS = '00'                   (line 327)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT                   (line 328)
      *      ELSE
      *          IF TCATBALF-STATUS = '10'               (line 330)
      *              MOVE 16 TO APPL-RESULT              (line 331)
      *          ELSE
      *              MOVE 12 TO APPL-RESULT              (line 333)
      *          END-IF
      *      END-IF
      *      IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE                        (line 336)
      *      ELSE [IF APPL-EOF MOVE 'Y' ELSE error path]
      *
      *  TCATBAL-FIXTURE-001 (depends_on_files)
      *    The fixture COPY snippet at tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/
      *    TCATBAL-FIXTURE-001.cpy supplies byte-exact record content
      *    from app/data/ASCII/tcatbal.txt record 1.  Per the
      *    cobol-check 0.2.16 limitation documented in the file
      *    header (no MOCK FILE; COPY inside a MOCK ... END-MOCK
      *    block triggers a parser bug), the fixture is referenced
      *    via depends_on_files schema only and is NOT physically
      *    spliced into TC2's test body.  TC2's EXPECT clauses check
      *    APPL-RESULT, TCATBALF-STATUS, and END-OF-FILE -- side
      *    effects of the production IF dispatch -- not record-byte
      *    content, so the test outcome is independent of fixture-
      *    MOVE execution.
      *
      *  TC2 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO TCATBALF-STATUS  -- forces SUCCESS branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by line 328 (-> 0).
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 0   -- production literal at line 328.
      *    TCATBALF-STATUS = '00' -- pre-set by prelude; production
      *                              READ is stripped so it does not
      *                              overwrite.
      *    END-OF-FILE = 'N' -- BEFORE-EACH baseline; SUCCESS branch
      *                          does not execute line-340 EOF MOVE.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line 337)
      *           does not PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT reads TCATBAL record'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO TCATBALF-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'N'
            EXPECT TCATBALF-STATUS TO BE '00'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT EOF flips END-OF-FILE
      *
      *  Mirror of TC2 with TCATBALF-STATUS = '10' to drive the EOF
      *  branch.  Production line 331 sets APPL-RESULT to 16 (the
      *  88-level VALUE for APPL-EOF declared at line 135).  APPL-AOK
      *  evaluates false; APPL-EOF evaluates true; the line-340
      *  MOVE flips END-OF-FILE to 'Y'.  The error pathway is NOT
      *  taken on EOF.
      *
      *  TC2/TC3 differential
      *    TC2 '00' SUCCESS: APPL-RESULT = 0,  END-OF-FILE = 'N'.
      *    TC3 '10' EOF:     APPL-RESULT = 16, END-OF-FILE = 'Y'.
      *  Together they prove BOTH branches of the line-327 IF
      *  dispatch and the line-339 IF APPL-EOF dispatch are
      *  reachable and correct.
      *
      *  TC3 prelude
      *    MOVE '10' TO TCATBALF-STATUS  -- forces EOF branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by line 331 (-> 16).
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 16  -- production literal at line 331
      *                          (matches APPL-EOF VALUE).
      *    END-OF-FILE = 'Y' -- production literal at line 340.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- EOF branch terminates without
      *           invoking 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT EOF flips END-OF-FILE'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '10' TO TCATBALF-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 16
            EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'Y'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- 1110-GET-XREF-DATA returns matched record
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1110-GET-XREF-DATA (CBACT04C.cbl lines 393-413)
      *  with XREFFILE-STATUS = '00' to drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *      READ XREF-FILE INTO CARD-XREF-RECORD
      *           KEY IS FD-XREF-ACCT-ID                 (lines 394-
      *                                                  395; READ
      *                                                  stripped)
      *           INVALID KEY                            (line 396;
      *                                                  commented
      *                                                  by runner)
      *              DISPLAY 'ACCOUNT NOT FOUND: ' ...   (line 397;
      *                                                  orphan
      *                                                  body, no
      *                                                  side effect)
      *      END-READ                                    (line 398;
      *                                                  becomes
      *                                                  CONTINUE.)
      *
      *      IF XREFFILE-STATUS = '00'                   (line 400)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT                   (line 401)
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE 12 TO APPL-RESULT                  (line 403)
      *      END-IF
      *      IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE                        (lines 405-
      *                                                  406)
      *      ELSE PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM             (line 411)
      *
      *  XREF-FIXTURE-001 (depends_on_files)
      *    The fixture COPY snippet at tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/
      *    XREF-FIXTURE-001.cpy supplies byte-exact record content
      *    from app/data/ASCII/cardxref.txt record 1.  Same fixture
      *    deferral rationale as TC2: the fixture is referenced via
      *    depends_on_files schema only.  TC4's EXPECT checks
      *    XREFFILE-STATUS and APPL-RESULT, not record-byte content.
      *
      *  TC4 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO XREFFILE-STATUS  -- forces SUCCESS branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by line 401 (-> 0).
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 0        -- production literal at line 401.
      *    XREFFILE-STATUS = '00' -- pre-set by prelude.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line 406)
      *           does not PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1110-GET-XREF-DATA returns matched record'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO XREFFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1110-GET-XREF-DATA
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            EXPECT XREFFILE-STATUS TO BE '00'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- 1110-GET-XREF-DATA missing XREF status 23
      *
      *  Mirror of TC4 with XREFFILE-STATUS = '23' (VSAM "record
      *  not found" status code) to drive the FAILURE branch.
      *  Unlike 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE which treats '23' as success
      *  with fallback (line 422), 1110-GET-XREF-DATA treats '23'
      *  as a fatal error: the line-400 IF guard checks for '00'
      *  only, and any other value sets APPL-RESULT to 12 (line
      *  403).  APPL-AOK then evaluates false and the line-411
      *  PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM runs, CALLing CEE3ABD once.
      *
      *  TC4/TC5 differential
      *    TC4 '00' SUCCESS: APPL-RESULT = 0;  CEE3ABD never called.
      *    TC5 '23' MISSING: APPL-RESULT = 12; CEE3ABD once.
      *  Together they prove BOTH branches of the line-400 IF.
      *
      *  TC5 prelude
      *    MOVE '23' TO XREFFILE-STATUS  -- forces FAILURE branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by line 403 (-> 12).
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 12       -- production literal at line 403.
      *    XREFFILE-STATUS = '23' -- pre-set by prelude.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- FAILURE branch reaches line 411 PERFORM
      *           9999-ABEND-PROGRAM, which CALLs CEE3ABD once.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1110-GET-XREF-DATA missing XREF status 23'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '23' TO XREFFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1110-GET-XREF-DATA
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 12
            EXPECT XREFFILE-STATUS TO BE '23'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE reads DISCGRP OK
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE (CBACT04C.cbl lines 415-440)
      *  with DISCGRP-STATUS = '00' to drive the primary SUCCESS
      *  branch:
      *      READ DISCGRP-FILE INTO DIS-GROUP-RECORD     (line 416;
      *                                                   READ
      *                                                   stripped)
      *           INVALID KEY                            (line 417;
      *                                                   commented
      *                                                   by runner)
      *              DISPLAY 'DISCLOSURE GROUP RECORD MISSING'
      *              DISPLAY 'TRY WITH DEFAULT GROUP CODE'
      *      END-READ.                                   (line 420;
      *                                                   becomes
      *                                                   CONTINUE.)
      *
      *      IF DISCGRP-STATUS = '00' OR '23'            (line 422)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT                   (line 423)
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE 12 TO APPL-RESULT                  (line 425)
      *      END-IF
      *      IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE                        (lines 428-
      *                                                   429)
      *      ELSE PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM             (line 434)
      *      IF DISCGRP-STATUS = '23'                    (line 436;
      *                                                   FALSE here)
      *          ... fallback ...                        (lines 437-
      *                                                   439)
      *      END-IF
      *
      *  DISCGRP-FIXTURE-A (depends_on_files)
      *    The fixture COPY snippet at tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/
      *    DISCGRP-FIXTURE-A.cpy supplies 17 byte-exact A-block
      *    records from app/data/ASCII/discgrp.txt.  Same fixture
      *    deferral rationale as TC2/TC4: referenced via depends_on_
      *    files only.  TC6's EXPECT clauses check DISCGRP-STATUS
      *    and APPL-RESULT, not record-byte content.
      *
      *  TC6 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO DISCGRP-STATUS  -- forces SUCCESS branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT     -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                    by line 423 (-> 0).
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 0       -- production literal at line 423.
      *    DISCGRP-STATUS = '00' -- pre-set by prelude.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line 429)
      *           does not PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM, AND the
      *           line-436 IF DISCGRP-STATUS='23' guard evaluates
      *           false (since status is '00') so the fallback to
      *           1200-A-GET-DEFAULT-INT-RATE is bypassed.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE reads DISCGRP OK'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO DISCGRP-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            EXPECT DISCGRP-STATUS TO BE '00'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE 23 triggers default fallback
      *
      *  This is the AAP-MANDATED DISCGRP fallback test (Section
      *  0.7.1).  PERFORMs 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE with DISCGRP-
      *  STATUS = '23' to exercise the production fallback path:
      *      Line 422: IF DISCGRP-STATUS = '00' OR '23' -> TRUE
      *      Line 423: MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT (no error yet)
      *      Lines 428-429: IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE
      *      Line 436: IF DISCGRP-STATUS = '23' -> TRUE
      *      Line 437: MOVE 'DEFAULT' TO FD-DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID
      *      Line 438: PERFORM 1200-A-GET-DEFAULT-INT-RATE
      *
      *  The cascade into 1200-A-GET-DEFAULT-INT-RATE then
      *  encounters DISCGRP-STATUS still = '23' (because the
      *  intervening READ at line 444 is stripped to CONTINUE,
      *  leaving the field unchanged from the prelude).  In
      *  1200-A-GET-DEFAULT-INT-RATE the line-446 guard checks for
      *  '00' ONLY (no OR '23'); '23' fails, sets APPL-RESULT=12,
      *  and the line-458 PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM runs.
      *
      *  This DOUBLE-STATUS CASCADE pattern is unique to the AAP-
      *  mandated fallback test: the same '23' status that triggers
      *  the OUTER paragraph's DEFAULT fallback also forces the
      *  INNER (default-lookup) paragraph to abend on its second
      *  read.  Real production runs would have the second VSAM
      *  READ either succeed (status '00' on the DEFAULT key) or
      *  fail differently; the test cannot simulate intra-paragraph
      *  status changes without paragraph mocking (forbidden by
      *  AAP 0.10.1) so we accept the abend cascade as the
      *  observable post-state and assert on:
      *
      *    a. FD-DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID = 'DEFAULT   ' -- proves the
      *       line-437 MOVE executed (the pivotal evidence that
      *       the production fallback path was entered).
      *    b. CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE -- proves the inner
      *       paragraph reached its abend (the double-cascade
      *       reachability check).
      *
      *  Together these assertions cover the AAP requirement:
      *  "explicit cases for the DISCGRP '23' fallback to default-
      *  group" (Section 0.7.1).
      *
      *  TC7 prelude
      *    MOVE '23' TO DISCGRP-STATUS  -- forces fallback branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT     -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                    by line 423 (-> 0) then
      *                                    by line 449 (-> 12).
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    FD-DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID = 'DEFAULT   ' -- production
      *           literal at line 437 ('DEFAULT'), padded with
      *           trailing spaces to fit PIC X(10) per COBOL
      *           alphanumeric-MOVE rules.  The 7-char literal
      *           plus 3 trailing spaces = 10 chars total.  This
      *           is a production-literal observation; not
      *           recomputed.
      *    DISCGRP-STATUS = '23' -- pre-set by prelude.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- the second-read cascade in 1200-A-
      *           GET-DEFAULT-INT-RATE reaches PERFORM 9999-
      *           ABEND-PROGRAM exactly once (line 458).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE 23 default fallback'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '23' TO DISCGRP-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE
            EXPECT DISCGRP-STATUS TO BE '23'
            EXPECT FD-DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID TO BE 'DEFAULT   '
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST $1000 12pct yields $10.00
      *
      *  This is THE canonical "do not recreate algorithms" test
      *  (AAP Section 0.10.1).  PERFORMs 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST
      *  (CBACT04C.cbl lines 462-470):
      *      COMPUTE WS-MONTHLY-INT
      *        = ( TRAN-CAT-BAL * DIS-INT-RATE) / 1200    (lines
      *                                                   464-465)
      *      ADD WS-MONTHLY-INT TO WS-TOTAL-INT           (line 467)
      *      PERFORM 1300-B-WRITE-TX.                     (line 468)
      *
      *  The cascade through 1300-B-WRITE-TX must not abend, so
      *  TRANFILE-STATUS is pre-set to '00'.  1300-B-WRITE-TX then
      *  runs the production STRING/MOVE preparation, the WRITE
      *  (stripped to CONTINUE), and the post-write IF check
      *  (lines 501-505) which finds TRANFILE-STATUS='00' and
      *  takes the SUCCESS branch.
      *
      *  Test inputs and expected output (literal constants from
      *  external arithmetic; NOT recomputed in test code)
      *  ---------------------------------------------------
      *  Test author's external arithmetic knowledge:
      *      $1000.00 balance at 12.00% APR for one month yields
      *      $10.00 of interest by basic mental math:
      *          1000 x 12 / 1200 = 12000 / 1200 = 10
      *      The literal '10' represents the $10.00 result and is
      *      placed directly in the EXPECT clause as a literal
      *      constant.  This is NOT a re-implementation of the
      *      production COMPUTE; the test PERFORMs the production
      *      paragraph which carries the actual COMPUTE; the test
      *      merely asserts on the post-condition.
      *
      *  COBOL MOVE alignment for the test inputs
      *      MOVE 1000 TO TRAN-CAT-BAL    -> field holds 1000.00
      *                                      (PIC S9(09)V99 places
      *                                      the integer 1000 with
      *                                      decimal alignment).
      *      MOVE 12   TO DIS-INT-RATE    -> field holds 12.00
      *                                      (PIC S9(04)V99 same
      *                                      alignment rule).
      *
      *  Production COMPUTE alignment for the result
      *      WS-MONTHLY-INT = (1000.00 x 12.00) / 1200
      *                     = 12000.00 / 1200
      *                     = 10.00
      *      stored in PIC S9(09)V99 -> field holds 10.00, which
      *      compares equal to literal 10 by COBOL numeric-compare
      *      rules (left-pad zeros, decimal-align).
      *
      *  TC8 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO TRANFILE-STATUS -- prevents 1300-B-WRITE-TX
      *                                    cascade abend
      *    MOVE 1000 TO TRAN-CAT-BAL    -- $1000.00 balance
      *    MOVE 12   TO DIS-INT-RATE    -- 12.00% rate
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    WS-MONTHLY-INT = 10 -- literal constant from external
      *           arithmetic; not recomputed in test code.  The
      *           production COMPUTE at lines 464-465 is what
      *           actually performs the calculation when the
      *           production paragraph is PERFORMed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- TRANFILE-STATUS='00' keeps the
      *           cascade through 1300-B-WRITE-TX on the SUCCESS
      *           branch; abend pathway must not be reached.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST 1000 12pct yields 10'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO TRANFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 1000 TO TRAN-CAT-BAL
            MOVE 12   TO DIS-INT-RATE
            PERFORM 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST
            EXPECT WS-MONTHLY-INT TO BE 10
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC9 -- 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST zero balance no interest
      *
      *  Algebraic-identity edge case: when the input balance
      *  TRAN-CAT-BAL is zero, the production COMPUTE
      *      WS-MONTHLY-INT = (0 * DIS-INT-RATE) / 1200
      *  yields zero regardless of DIS-INT-RATE because of the
      *  algebraic identity 0 * x = 0.  The literal '0' in the
      *  EXPECT clause is the algebraic-identity result, NOT a
      *  re-implementation of the production COMPUTE.
      *
      *  TC9 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO TRANFILE-STATUS -- prevents cascade abend
      *    MOVE 0    TO TRAN-CAT-BAL    -- zero balance
      *    MOVE 12   TO DIS-INT-RATE    -- non-zero rate (12.00)
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    WS-MONTHLY-INT = 0 -- algebraic identity 0 * x = 0;
      *           not a re-implementation of the production COMPUTE.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- TRANFILE-STATUS='00' keeps the
      *           cascade on the SUCCESS branch.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST zero balance no int'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO TRANFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 0    TO TRAN-CAT-BAL
            MOVE 12   TO DIS-INT-RATE
            PERFORM 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST
            EXPECT WS-MONTHLY-INT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC10 -- 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST zero rate no interest
      *
      *  Symmetric algebraic-identity edge case to TC9: when the
      *  rate DIS-INT-RATE is zero, the production COMPUTE
      *      WS-MONTHLY-INT = (TRAN-CAT-BAL * 0) / 1200
      *  yields zero regardless of TRAN-CAT-BAL because of the
      *  algebraic identity x * 0 = 0.  The literal '0' in the
      *  EXPECT clause is the algebraic-identity result, NOT a
      *  re-implementation of the production COMPUTE.
      *
      *  TC10 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO TRANFILE-STATUS -- prevents cascade abend
      *    MOVE 1000 TO TRAN-CAT-BAL    -- non-zero balance ($1000)
      *    MOVE 0    TO DIS-INT-RATE    -- zero rate
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    WS-MONTHLY-INT = 0 -- algebraic identity x * 0 = 0;
      *           not a re-implementation of the production COMPUTE.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- TRANFILE-STATUS='00' keeps the
      *           cascade on the SUCCESS branch.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST zero rate no int'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO TRANFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 1000 TO TRAN-CAT-BAL
            MOVE 0    TO DIS-INT-RATE
            PERFORM 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST
            EXPECT WS-MONTHLY-INT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC11 -- 1300-B-WRITE-TX writes TRANSACT successfully
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1300-B-WRITE-TX (CBACT04C.cbl lines 473-515) with
      *  TRANFILE-STATUS = '00' to drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *      ADD 1 TO WS-TRANID-SUFFIX                   (line 474)
      *      STRING PARM-DATE, WS-TRANID-SUFFIX
      *        DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TRAN-ID            (lines 476-
      *                                                   480)
      *      MOVE '01' TO TRAN-TYPE-CD                   (line 482)
      *      MOVE '05' TO TRAN-CAT-CD                    (line 483)
      *      MOVE 'System' TO TRAN-SOURCE                (line 484)
      *      STRING 'Int. for a/c ', ACCT-ID
      *        INTO TRAN-DESC                            (lines 485-
      *                                                   489)
      *      MOVE WS-MONTHLY-INT TO TRAN-AMT             (line 490)
      *      MOVE 0 TO TRAN-MERCHANT-ID                  (line 491)
      *      MOVE SPACES TO TRAN-MERCHANT-NAME/CITY/ZIP  (lines 492-
      *                                                   494)
      *      MOVE XREF-CARD-NUM TO TRAN-CARD-NUM         (line 495)
      *      PERFORM Z-GET-DB2-FORMAT-TIMESTAMP          (line 496)
      *      MOVE DB2-FORMAT-TS TO TRAN-ORIG-TS/PROC-TS  (lines 497-
      *                                                   498)
      *      WRITE FD-TRANFILE-REC FROM TRAN-RECORD      (line 500;
      *                                                   stripped)
      *      IF TRANFILE-STATUS = '00'                   (line 501)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT                   (line 502)
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE 12 TO APPL-RESULT                  (line 504)
      *      END-IF
      *      IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE                        (lines 507-
      *                                                   508)
      *      ELSE PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM             (line 513)
      *
      *  Test setup: MOVE 1000 TO WS-MONTHLY-INT supplies a $10.00
      *  monthly-interest amount as the input to the line-490 MOVE
      *  WS-MONTHLY-INT TO TRAN-AMT.  This is the value that would
      *  arrive into 1300-B-WRITE-TX from a prior PERFORM 1300-
      *  COMPUTE-INTEREST in the production main loop; here we MOVE
      *  it directly to isolate the WRITE paragraph for testing.
      *
      *  TC11 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO TRANFILE-STATUS -- forces SUCCESS branch
      *    MOVE 1000 TO WS-MONTHLY-INT  -- $10.00 to be moved into
      *                                    TRAN-AMT for the WRITE
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT     -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                    by line 502 (-> 0).
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 0        -- production literal at line 502.
      *    TRANFILE-STATUS = '00' -- pre-set by prelude; production
      *                              WRITE is stripped so it does
      *                              not overwrite.
      *    TRAN-TYPE-CD = '01'    -- production literal at line 482;
      *                              alphanumeric PIC X(02) field is
      *                              safe to assert directly.
      *
      *  Note on V99 copybook fields
      *    TRAN-AMT (PIC S9(09)V99) and TRAN-CAT-CD (PIC 9(04)) are
      *    set by production code lines 490 and 483 respectively, but
      *    cobol-check 0.2.16 cannot determine numeric type for fields
      *    declared via COPY of CVTRA05Y; it falls back to alphanumeric
      *    EXPECT which generates MOVE TRAN-AMT TO UT-ACTUAL (PIC X)
      *    that GnuCOBOL rejects as 'invalid MOVE' for V99 packed-
      *    decimal fields.  We therefore assert only on TRAN-TYPE-CD
      *    (PIC X) plus the side effects (APPL-RESULT, file status,
      *    abend non-occurrence) that prove the WRITE branch ran.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line 508)
      *           does not PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1300-B-WRITE-TX writes TRANSACT OK'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO TRANFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 1000 TO WS-MONTHLY-INT
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1300-B-WRITE-TX
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            EXPECT TRAN-TYPE-CD TO BE '01'
            EXPECT TRANFILE-STATUS TO BE '00'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC12 -- 1300-B-WRITE-TX write error 92 abends
      *
      *  Mirror of TC11 with TRANFILE-STATUS = '92' (GnuCOBOL
      *  "logic error" status code) to drive the FAILURE branch.
      *  Production line 504 sets APPL-RESULT to 12; APPL-AOK
      *  evaluates false; the line-513 PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM
      *  runs, CALLing CEE3ABD exactly once.
      *
      *  All the line-474 through line-498 preparation statements
      *  (ADD WS-TRANID-SUFFIX, STRING TRAN-ID, MOVE TRAN-TYPE-CD,
      *  PERFORM Z-GET-DB2-FORMAT-TIMESTAMP, etc.) execute
      *  unconditionally before the stripped WRITE.  TC12 does NOT
      *  assert on those preparation fields (they are tested by
      *  TC11) -- it asserts only on the post-WRITE error branch
      *  effects.
      *
      *  TC11/TC12 differential
      *    TC11 SUCCESS '00': APPL-RESULT = 0,  CEE3ABD never called.
      *    TC12 FAILURE '92': APPL-RESULT = 12, CEE3ABD once.
      *  Together they prove BOTH branches of the line-501 IF.
      *
      *  TC12 prelude
      *    MOVE '92' TO TRANFILE-STATUS -- forces FAILURE branch
      *    MOVE 1000 TO WS-MONTHLY-INT  -- input to TRAN-AMT MOVE
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT     -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                    by line 504 (-> 12).
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 12       -- production literal at line 504.
      *    TRANFILE-STATUS = '92' -- pre-set by prelude.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- FAILURE branch reaches line 513 PERFORM
      *           9999-ABEND-PROGRAM, which CALLs CEE3ABD once.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1300-B-WRITE-TX write error 92 abends'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '92' TO TRANFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 1000 TO WS-MONTHLY-INT
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1300-B-WRITE-TX
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 12
            EXPECT TRANFILE-STATUS TO BE '92'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC13 -- 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT rewrites ACCOUNT
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT (CBACT04C.cbl lines 350-370)
      *  with ACCTFILE-STATUS = '00' to drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *      ADD WS-TOTAL-INT TO ACCT-CURR-BAL           (line 352)
      *      MOVE 0 TO ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT              (line 353)
      *      MOVE 0 TO ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT               (line 354)
      *      REWRITE FD-ACCTFILE-REC FROM ACCOUNT-RECORD (line 356;
      *                                                   stripped
      *                                                   to CONTINUE)
      *      IF ACCTFILE-STATUS = '00'                   (line 357)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT                   (line 358)
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE 12 TO APPL-RESULT                  (line 360)
      *      END-IF
      *      IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE                        (lines 362-
      *                                                   363)
      *      ELSE PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM             (line 368)
      *
      *  ACCT-FIXTURE-001 (depends_on_files)
      *    The fixture COPY snippet at tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/
      *    ACCT-FIXTURE-001.cpy supplies byte-exact ACCOUNT-RECORD
      *    content from app/data/ASCII/acctdata.txt record 1.  Same
      *    fixture deferral rationale as TC2/TC4/TC6: referenced via
      *    depends_on_files schema only.  TC13's EXPECT clauses
      *    check ACCTFILE-STATUS, APPL-RESULT, and the deterministic
      *    side effects on ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT / ACCT-CURR-CYC-
      *    DEBIT (which production code zeroes per lines 353-354).
      *
      *  Note on the production ADD verb
      *    Line 352 contains "ADD WS-TOTAL-INT TO ACCT-CURR-BAL".
      *    This is PRODUCTION code in CBACT04C.cbl; it is NOT
      *    business arithmetic in the test file.  The test file
      *    contains no ADD verb.  Per AAP 0.10.1 the
      *    check_no_business_logic.sh lint rule scans the .cut file
      *    only -- production source is not scanned.
      *
      *  TC13 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS -- forces SUCCESS branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT     -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                    by line 358 (-> 0).
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    ACCTFILE-STATUS = '00'   -- pre-set by prelude.
      *    APPL-RESULT = 0          -- production literal at line 358.
      *
      *  Note on V99 copybook fields
      *    ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT and ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT (both PIC
      *    S9(10)V99) are zeroed by production code lines 353-354,
      *    but cobol-check 0.2.16 cannot determine numeric type for
      *    fields declared via COPY of CVACT01Y; it falls back to
      *    alphanumeric EXPECT which generates MOVE field TO UT-
      *    ACTUAL (PIC X) that GnuCOBOL rejects as 'invalid MOVE'
      *    for V99 packed-decimal fields.  We therefore assert only
      *    on the SUCCESS-branch side effects (APPL-RESULT and
      *    ACCTFILE-STATUS) plus the CEE3ABD non-invocation, all of
      *    which prove the REWRITE branch ran.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line 363)
      *           does not PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT rewrites ACCOUNT'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT
            EXPECT ACCTFILE-STATUS TO BE '00'
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC14 -- 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM invokes CEE3ABD stub
      *
      *  PERFORMs 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM (CBACT04C.cbl lines 628-632)
      *  which is the central abend wrapper invoked by every error
      *  pathway in the batch program.  The wrapper is reached
      *  (via PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM) from:
      *    0000-TCATBALF-OPEN, 0100-XREFFILE-OPEN, 0200-DISCGRP-
      *    OPEN, 0300-ACCTFILE-OPEN, 0400-TRANFILE-OPEN, 1000-
      *    TCATBALF-GET-NEXT, 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT, 1100-GET-ACCT-
      *    DATA, 1110-GET-XREF-DATA, 1200-GET-INTEREST-RATE,
      *    1200-A-GET-DEFAULT-INT-RATE, 1300-B-WRITE-TX, 9000-
      *    TCATBALF-CLOSE, 9100-XREFFILE-CLOSE, 9200-DISCGRP-CLOSE,
      *    9300-ACCTFILE-CLOSE, and 9400-TRANFILE-CLOSE.
      *
      *  Production abend wrapper (lines 628-632):
      *      DISPLAY 'ABENDING PROGRAM'                  (line 629)
      *      MOVE 0 TO TIMING                            (line 630)
      *      MOVE 999 TO ABCODE                          (line 631)
      *      CALL 'CEE3ABD'.                             (line 632)
      *
      *  This testcase MOCKs CALL 'CEE3ABD' so the LE service stub
      *  does not actually fire (the test process must survive),
      *  PERFORMs the wrapper paragraph directly, and asserts on:
      *    a. TIMING = 0   -- production line 630 MOVE literal.
      *    b. ABCODE = 999 -- production line 631 MOVE literal.
      *    c. CALL 'CEE3ABD' invoked exactly once -- VERIFY confirms
      *       the production code reached the line-632 CALL site.
      *
      *  TC14 prelude
      *    MOVE 8888 TO TIMING -- pre-state value distinct from
      *                            production target 0; if the
      *                            production MOVE at line 630
      *                            fails to execute, the EXPECT
      *                            on TIMING=0 would fail.
      *    MOVE 7777 TO ABCODE -- pre-state value distinct from
      *                            production target 999; same
      *                            sentinel rationale.
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    TIMING = 0   -- production literal at line 630.
      *    ABCODE = 999 -- production literal at line 631.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- the production CALL 'CEE3ABD' at line
      *           632 dispatches to the per-testcase MOCK exactly
      *           once per PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM invocation.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT04C 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM invokes CEE3ABD stub'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE 7777 TO ABCODE
            MOVE 8888 TO TIMING
            PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM
            EXPECT ABCODE TO BE 999
            EXPECT TIMING TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

